<title>ROMANIA: ROMANIA FORAJ HAD HIGHER PROFIT IN 1996.</title>
<headline>ROMANIA FORAJ HAD HIGHER PROFIT IN 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>					  (billion of leu unless stated)</p>
<p> Gross profit			     1.63     vs     1.37</p>
<p> Net profit				 1.63     vs    738 mln</p>
<p> Turnover				  30.66     vs    22.86</p>
<p> Fixed assets			    14.10     vs    12.72</p>
<p> Current assets			  10.84     vs     7.26</p>
<p> Total assets			    25.67     vs    20.79</p>
<p> Share capital			   16.53     vs    14.37</p>
<p> Total debts				5.76     vs     3.72</p>
<p> Total dividends			  585 mln  vs    n.a.</p>
<p> Dividend per share - net	     31 lei   vs    n.a.</p>
<p>NOTE -- Foraj Sonde Craiova is a state-run oil</p>
<p>drilling company listed on the Bucharest bourse's second tier.</p>
<p>Data, reported to the exchange, are in nominal terms and in</p>
<p>line with Romanian accounting standards. Foraj raised its share</p>
<p>capital last year after adding terrain to it.</p>
<p>($=7,090 lei)</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
</text>
